    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217-a1">

                <pb facs="0208" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg134"/>

                <head>Sir James Hope to the
                        Secretary of the Admiralty</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Duncan at Trinidad,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 8, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> You will be pleased to acquaint the lords
                    commissioners of the admiralty, in reply to your letter of the 16th ultimo, that
                    in conversation with the governor of Demarara, on the subject of the alleged
                    attempt to seize United States steam vessels in the Pacific, he expressed his
                    intention of taking every means in his power to frustrate this scheme should any
                    attempt be made to carry it into execution, and that the senior officer of the
                    division will be directed to afford him every assistance for this purpose.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HOPE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of the Admiralty.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
